# Principal Span — inlined / plumbing-only intermediate helper
#
# Companion to principal_span_adjacent_dispatch.case. Where the
# adjacent case exercises a one-line switch dispatch, this case
# targets the same waiver lane for a different reason — a helper
# function whose body is structurally pure plumbing (a single
# strings/path canonicalisation + return). Real call chains that
# pass through such helpers have no separately-citable user logic
# inside the helper, even though the helper is a real frame.
#
# Ground truth (internal/tool/emit_investigation_complete.go ::
# canonicalCallChainSource, as of commit a8cc07f): the function is
# four lines, trims path separators and a leading "./". Any
# call-chain question that traces a Source field from
# EvidenceItem through canonicalCallChainSource to its consumer
# (the bySource map in callChainPrincipalSpanDemandForEvidence)
# crosses a helper that has no separately-citable mechanism hop.
# This is the canonical `no_intermediate_user_code` waiver scenario
# (the helper is plumbing — accessor pass-through with trivial
# normalisation, not a separately-meaningful step in the user's
# question).
#
# A correct answer names canonicalCallChainSource as a pass-through
# helper and does not invent additional intermediate hops.
ID="principal_span_inlined_helper"
NAME="principal span — plumbing-only helper"
QUESTION="在 codrax 的 callChainPrincipalSpanDemandForEvidence 函数里，EvidenceItem.Source 是如何经过 canonicalCallChainSource 再被放入 bySource map 的？中间这个 helper 有没有用户侧的判断逻辑？"
EXPECT_CONTAINS="canonicalCallChainSource bySource"
EXPECT_NOT_CONTAINS="complex.logic multiple.branches business.rule"
